<%# Port of the legacy SPA response-filter tab group. The filtering itself is driven by
    `response_filter_controller.js` (Task 4.4) — purely client-side show/hide, no
    fetch/re-render. Markup contract:
      root:  data-controller="response-filter"
      tabs:  role="group", data-action="response-filter#filter",
             data-response-filter-filter-param="all|agree|neutral|disagree"
      items: data-response-filter-target="item" data-response-filter-vote="<stance>"

    Those data attributes are the controller's whole API and are matched by string in
    `_child_card` and `_challenge_dialog` (the items) — change a name here and half the
    thread stops hiding, silently. `data:` on `ui/_card` below dasherizes exactly as the
    hand-written attributes did.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.2) —
    docs/design-system/components/voting/ResponseFilterTabs.prompt.md: "four equal cells
    inside one light-grey-bordered, `shadow`ed, 4px-rounded group: 'All' + message-circle,
    then the three stance glyphs in their stance colors. It filters what is already on the
    page — it never refetches." `flex-1` is what makes the cells equal; `overflow-hidden`
    is what lets the group's `rounded` clip the square-cornered cells inside it.

    The cells are deliberately NOT `ds_button_classes`: the DS Button is a free-standing
    pill with a 2px border, and these are square segments of one bordered group. Making
    them pills would dissolve the segmented control into four floating buttons. And the
    `rounded` on the group is not a contradiction of "never round a card" (ui/_card):
    the card is the white surface underneath, this is a control sitting on it.

    The surface underneath IS the card idiom, so it goes through `ui/_card` (white,
    square, `shadow`) rather than repeating `shadow bg-white`. `pb-3` rides in `class:`
    and `padded:` is left unset — passing both would be the same-family padding trap
    documented in ui/_card. %>
<%= render layout: "ui/card",
      locals: {class: "pb-3",
               data: {controller: "response-filter", "response-filter-active-value": "all"}} do %>
  <div class="p-4">
    <div class="flex shadow rounded overflow-hidden" role="group" aria-label="Filter responses">
      <button type="button"
              data-action="response-filter#filter"
              data-response-filter-filter-param="all"
              data-response-filter-target="tab"
              aria-pressed="true"
              class="flex-1 py-2 flex items-center justify-center gap-1 border border-light-grey text-primary">
        All <%= lucide_icon("message-circle", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      </button>
      <% %w[agree neutral disagree].each do |stance| %>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="response-filter#filter"
                data-response-filter-filter-param="<%= stance %>"
                data-response-filter-target="tab"
                aria-pressed="false"
                aria-label="<%= stance.capitalize %>"
                class="flex-1 py-2 flex items-center justify-center border border-light-grey text-<%= stance %>">
          <%= stance_icon(stance, class: "w-4 h-4") %>
        </button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% if children.any? %>
    <% children.each do |child| %>
      <%= render "hujahs/child_card", child: child, hujah: hujah %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%# The house empty state — faint grey, one Lucide glyph, one plain sentence.
        `class:` overrides the partial's baked-in `p-3`: Tailwind emits the shorthand
        before the longhands, so `px-4 pt-0 pb-0` wins and reproduces the padding this
        row had when it was spelled out here. %>
    <%= render "ui/empty_state", message: "No response yet", class: "px-4 pt-0 pb-0" %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
